mixin () {
  // Static Markdown documentation of the backend's public API. Reads no state.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let doc = "# Restaurant Ordering Backend API\n\nThis canister powers a restaurant website: it serves the menu, accepts delivery\norders paid by cash or card, and lets an administrator review and manage\nincoming orders from an admin dashboard.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### Menu\n\n- `listDishes() : async [Dish]` — query. Returns every dish on the menu, sorted\n  ascending by `id`. Public: callable by anyone, including anonymous callers.\n- `getDish(id : DishId) : async ?Dish` — query. Returns the dish with the given\n  `id`, or `null` when no such dish exists. Public.\n\n### Orders\n\n- `placeOrder(customerName, phone, address, items, paymentMethod, cardholderName)\n  : async { #ok : Order; #err : PlaceOrderError }` — update. Validates the\n  request, prices every line item from the current menu, computes the subtotal,\n  delivery fee and total, assigns an order reference, persists the order with\n  status `#placed`, and returns it. Callable by anyone, including anonymous\n  callers; orders are not tied to a caller identity.\n- `listOrders() : async [Order]` — query. Returns every placed order, newest\n  first (descending `id`). **Admin only**: a non-admin caller traps with\n  `Unauthorized: Only admins can list orders`.\n- `updateOrderStatus(orderId : OrderId, newStatus : OrderStatus)\n  : async { #ok : Order; #err : UpdateOrderStatusError }` — update. **Admin\n  only**: a non-admin caller traps with\n  `Unauthorized: Only admins can update orders`. Applies an allowed status\n  transition to an existing order and returns the updated order, or a typed\n  error. Used by the admin dashboard to confirm, deliver or cancel an order.\n\n### Access control\n\n- `_initialize_access_control() : async ()` — update. Registers the caller. The\n  first non-anonymous caller to register becomes `#admin`; every later caller\n  becomes `#user`. Anonymous callers are ignored (no role is recorded).\n- `getCallerUserRole() : async UserRole` — query. Returns the caller's role:\n  `#guest` for anonymous callers, otherwise the stored role. Traps with\n  `User is not registered` when a signed-in caller has never registered.\n- `isCallerAdmin() : async Bool` — query. `true` only when the caller's stored\n  role is `#admin`.\n- `assignCallerUserRole(user : Principal, role : UserRole) : async ()` — update.\n  Admin only; assigns `role` to `user`. A non-admin caller traps with\n  `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles`.\n- `_internet_identity_sign_in_start() : async Blob` and\n  `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish() : async Result<(), Verify.Error>` —\n  Internet Identity sign-in handshake used by the frontend.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n`listDishes`, `getDish` and `placeOrder` require no authentication. `listOrders`\nand `updateOrderStatus` require an admin role, and the role-assignment method\nrequires an admin caller.\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds\nthe user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal\nagainst that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\nRegistration is a prerequisite for role-guarded calls. A direct API caller\nregisters by calling `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller\nbefore any role-guarded call, including guarded queries. The first initializer\nreceives `#admin`; every subsequent caller receives `#user`. An unregistered\nsigned-in caller receives the trap `User is not registered` from\n`getCallerUserRole` and `isCallerAdmin`, and a non-admin caller receives\n`Unauthorized: Only admins can list orders` from `listOrders` or\n`Unauthorized: Only admins can update orders` from `updateOrderStatus`.\nAnonymous callers receive `#guest` from `getCallerUserRole` and `false` from\n`isCallerAdmin`.\n\nA caller can be unregistered even when the app already knows it: registration\nhappens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a\nprincipal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's\nowner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different\nprincipal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- All monetary amounts (`price`, `unitPrice`, `subtotal`, `deliveryFee`,\n  `total`) are `Nat` values in **minor currency units (cents)**. A price of\n  `1199` means 11.99.\n- `createdAt` is a `Timestamp` (`Int`), nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, as\n  returned by `Time.now()`.\n- `DishId` and `OrderId` are `Nat`.\n- `Category` is the variant `#starters | #mains | #desserts | #drinks`.\n- `PaymentMethod` is the variant `#cash | #card`.\n- `OrderStatus` is the variant `#placed | #confirmed | #delivered | #cancelled`.\n  New orders are always created with status `#placed`.\n- `cardholderName` is `?Text`: present only for `#card` orders, `null` for cash.\n- `address` is a record `{ street; city; postcode; notes }`; all fields are\n  `Text`, and `notes` may be empty.\n- `items` is an array of `{ dishId; name; unitPrice; quantity }`. `name` and\n  `unitPrice` are captured from the menu at order time, so a later menu price\n  change does not alter an existing order.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n`placeOrder` is synchronous: a successful call returns the fully persisted\norder, including its `reference` (for example `ORD-000042`) and `id`. There is\nno asynchronous processing to poll. `listOrders` reflects every order placed so\nfar, newest first; poll it to observe new orders and their current status.\n\nOrder status changes only through `updateOrderStatus`, which is admin-only. The\nallowed transitions are:\n\n- `#placed` → `#confirmed` or `#cancelled`\n- `#confirmed` → `#delivered` or `#cancelled`\n- `#delivered` and `#cancelled` are terminal — no further transition is allowed.\n\nA transition that is not in this list is rejected with\n`#err(#invalidTransition({ from; to }))` and the stored order is left unchanged.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n`placeOrder` is **not idempotent**. Every successful call consumes a new\n`nextOrderId` and stores a new order, so retrying a call that actually succeeded\ncreates a duplicate order with a different reference. Retry only when the call\nfailed or its outcome is unknown, and reconcile against `listOrders` (admin) or\nthe returned reference before retrying.\n\n`updateOrderStatus` is **not idempotent** in general: re-applying the same\n`newStatus` to an order already in that status is rejected as an invalid\ntransition (for example `#confirmed` → `#confirmed`), because a status is never\nits own allowed successor. A retry after a successful call therefore returns\n`#err(#invalidTransition(...))` rather than `#ok`; treat that error as evidence\nthe change already landed and re-read the order via `listOrders` instead of\nretrying. `_initialize_access_control` is idempotent for an already-registered\ncaller (it leaves the existing role unchanged). `assignCallerUserRole`\noverwrites the target principal's role and is safe to repeat.\n\n## Errors, traps and gotchas\n\n`placeOrder` reports caller-actionable failures as `#err(PlaceOrderError)` rather\nthan trapping. The variants are:\n\n- `#emptyCart` — `items` is empty.\n- `#missingCustomerName` — `customerName` is blank or whitespace only.\n- `#missingPhone` — `phone` is blank or whitespace only.\n- `#missingAddress` — `street`, `city` or `postcode` is blank or whitespace only.\n- `#missingCardholderName` — `paymentMethod` is `#card` but `cardholderName` is\n  `null` or blank.\n- `#unknownDish(dishId)` — an item references a dish id that does not exist.\n- `#dishUnavailable(dishId)` — an item references a dish whose `available` flag\n  is `false`.\n\n`updateOrderStatus` reports caller-actionable failures as\n`#err(UpdateOrderStatusError)` rather than trapping. The variants are:\n\n- `#notFound(orderId)` — no order with that `id` exists.\n- `#unauthorized` — reserved for an authorization failure surfaced as a value;\n  in the current implementation a non-admin caller traps before this variant is\n  produced.\n- `#invalidTransition({ from; to })` — the requested change is not an allowed\n  transition from the order's current status.\n\nPricing rules: the delivery fee is a flat 399 cents, waived when the subtotal is\nat least 5000 cents. `total = subtotal + deliveryFee`. Line prices always come\nfrom the current menu, never from the client-supplied `unitPrice`.\n\nOther gotchas:\n\n- `listOrders`, `updateOrderStatus` and `assignCallerUserRole` trap (they do not\n  return an error variant) when the caller lacks the admin role.\n- `getCallerUserRole` traps for a signed-in but unregistered caller; use\n  `isCallerAdmin` when you only need a boolean and want `false` instead of a\n  trap.\n- Card payment is recorded as a payment method only. No card details are\n  collected, stored or charged by this backend.\n- The menu is seeded on first run and is read-only through the public API; there\n  is no public endpoint to add, edit or remove dishes.\n";
    doc
  };
};
